Vikram and Betal: The Truthful Child (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100129

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a child who always spoke the truth,” said Betal. “He never told a lie, even when he was afraid.”

One day, while playing, he accidentally broke a pot in his house.

His parents asked, “Who broke the pot?”

The child was scared but said, “I did.”

His parents were surprised but did not punish him.

Instead, they said, “We are proud of you for telling the truth.”

Later, the king heard about the child.

He called him and said, “Honesty like yours is rare.”

The king rewarded the child.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the child get a reward even after making a mistake?”

Vikram replied, “Because telling the truth is more important than hiding a mistake.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always tell the truth, even when it is difficult.
